# Plain HTTP on Caddy's port 80, which the release's compose.yml publishes on
# the host port CADDY_HTTP_PORT names. The host matcher ignores the port, so
# requests to localhost:<that port> land here.
#
# The prerenderer resolves `localhost` to its own container, so the site also
# answers to its compose service name, and that name is the render origin.

http://localhost, http://tt-caddy {
    import base.Caddyfile http://tt-caddy
}
